# Uploads — Cloudinary-backed images.
#
# Cloudinary is the only image backend; Azure Blob Storage is retired. The
# stored record is a convenience index, not the source of truth — Cloudinary is.
#
# POST /uploads accepts either an admin JWT or the pipeline's x-api-key, so the
# blog workflow can upload banners without holding a user account.
#
# v1's /upload is not aliased — see the last request for what it returns now.
#
# These requests hit Cloudinary for real. With no credentials configured they
# return 503 upload_failed, which is the correct answer, not a broken file.

# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{adminEmail}}", "password": "{{adminPassword}}" }

###

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.access_token}}

### Upload an image.
# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HttpFileBoundary

------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="example.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/example.png
------HttpFileBoundary--

###

@publicId = {{upload.response.body.$.publicId}}

### Upload into a folder, with a deterministic public_id.
# Passing public_id is what makes a re-upload replace the asset rather than
# pile up a second copy — the blog pipeline derives it from the repo path.
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HttpFileBoundary

------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="example.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/example.png
------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="folder"

blog
------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="public_id"

blog/example-post-banner
------HttpFileBoundary--

### The same request again replaces the asset instead of duplicating it.
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HttpFileBoundary

------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="example.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/example.png
------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="public_id"

blog/example-post-banner
------HttpFileBoundary--

### Upload with the pipeline's API key instead of a JWT.
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads
x-api-key: {{blogSyncApiKey}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HttpFileBoundary

------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="example.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/example.png
------HttpFileBoundary--

### List what has been uploaded. Admin only.
GET {{baseUrl}}/uploads
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### List one folder.
GET {{baseUrl}}/uploads?folder=blog
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete. The public id is a path segment because Cloudinary ids contain
# slashes, so `blog/example-post-banner` goes in unescaped.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/uploads/{{publicId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

# ============================= failure cases =============================

### A non-image -> 400 unsupported_image_type, naming what is accepted.
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HttpFileBoundary

------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

not an image
------HttpFileBoundary--

### No credentials at all -> 401.
POST {{baseUrl}}/uploads
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HttpFileBoundary

------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="example.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/example.png
------HttpFileBoundary--

### An unknown public id -> 404.
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/uploads/nothing/here
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### v1's /upload is gone -> 404. Nothing should still be calling this.
POST {{baseUrl}}/upload
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----HttpFileBoundary

------HttpFileBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="example.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./fixtures/example.png
------HttpFileBoundary--
